    ["#A04000", "Rust-coloured sputum with fever and pleuritic pain", "Pneumococcal pneumonia", ["Tuberculosis", "Lung cancer", "Bronchitis"], "Classic of lobar pneumonia from Streptococcus pneumoniae. Vaccines help prevent it."],
    ["#C0392B", "Red-currant-jelly sputum in an older person who drinks heavily", "Klebsiella pneumonia", ["Tuberculosis", "Pulmonary embolism", "Asthma"], "Thick, bloody sputum. Often in alcohol use disorder or diabetes."],
    ["#D7BDE2", "Lilac, thickened patches on the skin with a purple edge", "Morphoea (localised scleroderma)", ["Bruise", "Eczema", "Vitiligo"], "Skin-only scleroderma. The lilac ring marks active inflammation."],
    ["#FAD02E", "Yellow-white raised spots on the face of a newborn", "Milia", ["Acne", "Chickenpox", "Thrush"], "Tiny keratin cysts. Harmless and gone within weeks. Don’t squeeze."],
    ["#FFB6C1", "A pink-orange stain in a newborn’s nappy", "Urate crystals (‘brick dust’)", ["Blood in the urine", "Infection", "Beetroot"], "Common in the first days before feeding is established. If persistent, check feeding and hydration."],
    ["#4A235A", "Dark bruising around both eyes a day after a head injury", "Basal skull fracture (‘raccoon eyes’)", ["Allergies", "Lack of sleep", "Sinusitis"], "Blood tracks from the skull base into the eye sockets. Ask about clear fluid from the nose or ears. CT needed."],
    ["#D4AC0D", "Thick, crumbly, yellow-brown toenails", "Fungal nail infection (onychomycosis)", ["Psoriasis", "Yellow nail syndrome", "Smoking"], "Confirm with clippings before months of treatment: psoriasis can look identical."],
    ["#7D3C98", "Purple, swollen gums that bleed, and corkscrew-shaped hairs", "Scurvy (vitamin C deficiency)", ["Gum disease", "Leukaemia", "Lichen planus"], "Still seen with very restricted diets. Vitamin C is needed to make collagen. Sailors once carried limes for this reason."],
    ["#1B2631", "A blue-black patch under a big toenail after a long run", "Subungual haematoma", ["Melanoma", "Fungal nail", "Splinter haemorrhage"], "Blood under the nail. It grows out with the nail; a streak that doesn’t needs a melanoma check."],
    ["#F4D03F", "Small yellow spots at the back of the eye in an older person", "Drusen (early macular degeneration)", ["Cataract", "Diabetic retinopathy", "Glaucoma"], "Deposits under the retina. Stop smoking; check central vision with an Amsler grid."],
    ["#E74C3C", "Cherry-red skin, headache and confusion in a family sharing a house with a faulty heater", "Carbon monoxide poisoning", ["Flu", "Food poisoning", "Sunburn"], "Cherry-red colour is a late and unreliable sign. Pulse oximeters read falsely normal; check a blood gas with CO-oximetry."],
    ["#CB4335", "Hot, red, swollen shin with a sharp, raised edge and a fever", "Erysipelas", ["Gout", "Deep vein thrombosis", "Eczema"], "A superficial strep infection of the skin. The crisp edge sets it apart from deeper cellulitis."],
    ["#E35D5B", "Bright red ‘slapped’ cheeks, then a lacy rash on the arms in a child who feels well", "Parvovirus B19 (fifth disease)", ["Scarlet fever", "Measles", "Sunburn"], "Usually mild, but tell pregnant contacts: it can affect the unborn baby."],
    ["#EC7063", "Red target-shaped spots on the palms a week after a cold sore", "Erythema multiforme", ["Hand, foot and mouth disease", "Scabies", "Measles"], "Usually triggered by herpes simplex. Targets have three rings. Settles by itself in a few weeks."],
    ["#F1948A", "Small red bumps and scale around the mouth and nose, sparing a thin rim at the lip edge", "Perioral dermatitis", ["Acne", "Eczema", "Impetigo"], "Often follows steroid creams on the face. Stop the steroid; it may flare first."],
    ["#E6564B", "Red cheeks and nose with flushing and pimples, but no blackheads", "Rosacea", ["Acne", "Lupus", "Sunburn"], "No blackheads (comedones) sets it apart from acne. Triggers include heat, alcohol and spicy food."],
    ["#FF6F61", "Itchy red welts that move around, each lasting less than a day", "Urticaria (hives)", ["Scabies", "Eczema", "Cellulitis"], "Individual welts come and go within 24 hours. Antihistamines are first line."],
    ["#C0392B", "Red flushed face, headache and diarrhoea within an hour of eating tuna steak", "Scombroid poisoning", ["Seafood allergy", "Food poisoning (salmonella)", "Ciguatera"], "Histamine builds up in badly stored fish. Antihistamines work; it isn’t an allergy."],
    ["#922B21", "Red, blistering rash and sore mouth and eyes two weeks after starting lamotrigine", "Stevens–Johnson syndrome", ["Chickenpox", "Hand, foot and mouth disease", "Sunburn"], "A skin emergency. Stop the drug and get to hospital; eye checks are urgent."],
    ["#B03A2E", "Red-purple spots that don’t fade under a glass, in a feverish, drowsy child", "Meningococcal sepsis", ["Viral rash", "Bruising", "Allergy"], "Non-blanching rash plus fever needs IV antibiotics now, before tests."],
    ["#F5B7B1", "A little blood in the nappy of a 5-day-old baby girl", "Newborn withdrawal bleed (pseudomenses)", ["Urinary tract infection", "Bowel bleeding", "Injury"], "Mum’s hormones drop after birth. Harmless and settles in a few days."],
    ["#CB4335", "Coral-red glow under a Wood’s lamp in a brown, scaly groin rash", "Erythrasma", ["Tinea cruris", "Psoriasis", "Candida"], "A Corynebacterium infection. Bacteria make porphyrins that glow coral red."],
    ["#E74C3C", "Red, swollen, painful ear that spares the earlobe, on both sides", "Relapsing polychondritis", ["Ear infection", "Cellulitis", "Gout"], "Cartilage is inflamed, and the lobe has none. Can also affect the nose, airway and eyes."],
    ["#E67E22", "Oily orange spotting on underwear after starting a weight-loss tablet", "Orlistat", ["Bowel infection", "Haemorrhoids", "Bile acid diarrhoea"], "Orlistat blocks fat absorption; the undigested fat leaks out. Less fat in the diet means fewer accidents."],
    ["#D35400", "Orange-brown spots like cayenne pepper in patches on both shins", "Pigmented purpuric dermatosis (Schamberg disease)", ["Vasculitis", "Low platelets", "Bruising"], "Leaky capillaries leave iron behind. Harmless, though it can last years."],
    ["#E8743B", "Orange-red skin of the palms with thick scale and ‘islands’ of normal skin", "Pityriasis rubra pilaris", ["Psoriasis", "Eczema", "Carotenaemia"], "A rare scaly skin condition. The islands of sparing are the clue."],
    ["#EB984E", "Orange-tan skin colour that won’t fade, in someone drinking litres of tomato juice", "Lycopenaemia", ["Jaundice", "Addison’s disease", "Carotenaemia"], "Lycopene from tomatoes stains the skin, like carotene from carrots. Eyes stay white."],
    ["#F39C12", "Yellow-orange shiny plaques on the shins of a woman with diabetes", "Necrobiosis lipoidica", ["Shin bruising", "Psoriasis", "Pretibial myxoedema"], "Often painless and can ulcerate. Linked with diabetes but can occur without it."],
    ["#A04000", "Red-brown skin and orange tears in a man treated for leprosy", "Clofazimine", ["Rifampicin", "Jaundice", "Addison’s disease"], "Clofazimine deposits in the skin. It fades slowly after stopping."],
    ["#F4D03F", "Neon-yellow urine after a multivitamin", "Riboflavin (vitamin B2)", ["Dehydration", "Jaundice", "Kidney disease"], "Riboflavin fluoresces yellow. Harmless."],
    ["#F7DC6F", "Thick yellow greasy scale on a baby’s scalp", "Cradle cap (infant seborrhoeic dermatitis)", ["Eczema", "Ringworm", "Psoriasis"], "Harmless. Soften with oil and brush gently. Usually gone by 12 months."],
    ["#F1C40F", "A bulging, yellow eardrum in a feverish toddler pulling at the ear", "Acute otitis media", ["Earwax", "Swimmer’s ear", "Glue ear"], "A bulging drum is the most reliable sign. Many settle without antibiotics."],
    ["#F9E79F", "Painful round yellow-grey mouth ulcer with a red halo", "Aphthous ulcer", ["Oral cancer", "Herpes", "Thrush"], "Common and recurrent. One lasting over 3 weeks needs checking."],
    ["#D4AC0D", "Yellow skin in a newborn within the first 24 hours of life", "Pathological jaundice (often blood group haemolysis)", ["Normal newborn jaundice", "Breast milk jaundice", "Gilbert syndrome"], "Jaundice in the first day is never normal. Check bilirubin and blood group urgently."],
    ["#F4D03F", "Yellow-orange streaks in the creases of the palms", "Palmar xanthomas (type III dyslipidaemia)", ["Carotenaemia", "Jaundice", "Calluses"], "A clue to dysbetalipoproteinaemia, a rare inherited lipid disorder with high heart risk."],
    ["#F7DC6F", "A yellowish raised bump on the white of the eye beside the cornea", "Pinguecula", ["Melanoma of the eye", "Conjunctivitis", "Arcus senilis"], "Sun and wind damage. Harmless; lubricating drops help irritation."],
    ["#F5B041", "Thick yellow discharge from the penis and burning when weeing", "Gonorrhoea", ["Chlamydia only", "Urinary tract infection", "Thrush"], "Test with a swab and urine PCR. Treat with ceftriaxone and notify partners."],
    ["#C9A227", "Frothy yellow-green, fishy discharge with a ‘strawberry’ cervix", "Trichomoniasis", ["Bacterial vaginosis", "Thrush", "Gonorrhoea"], "A parasite. Treat with metronidazole, and treat partners too."],
    ["#F9E79F", "Yellow fluid in the CSF 12 hours after a thunderclap headache", "Xanthochromia (subarachnoid haemorrhage)", ["Meningitis", "Traumatic tap", "Normal CSF"], "Red cells break down to bilirubin, which takes hours. That’s why the LP is timed 12 hours after onset."],
    ["#27AE60", "Green, sticky ‘tar’ in a newborn’s first nappies", "Meconium", ["Bile vomit", "Infection", "Blood"], "Normal first poo. No meconium by 48 hours raises concern for Hirschsprung disease or cystic fibrosis."],
    ["#2E8B57", "Green amniotic fluid when the waters break at 41 weeks", "Meconium-stained liquor", ["Infection", "Bleeding", "Normal"], "Common after term. Thick meconium can signal distress; the baby is watched closely."],
    ["#52BE80", "A bruise that has turned green and yellow after a week", "Healing bruise (biliverdin and bilirubin)", ["Infection", "Bleeding disorder", "Jaundice"], "Haemoglobin breaks down to green biliverdin, then yellow bilirubin. You can’t reliably date a bruise by colour."],
    ["#1ABC9C", "Blue-green glow under a Wood’s lamp in a child’s scaly scalp patch", "Tinea capitis (Microsporum)", ["Psoriasis", "Alopecia areata", "Cradle cap"], "Needs oral antifungals; creams don’t reach the hair roots. The common Trichophyton type doesn’t glow."],
    ["#16A085", "A bright green-yellow streak on the cornea after fluorescein drops and a scratch from a twig", "Corneal abrasion", ["Glaucoma", "Conjunctivitis", "Retinal detachment"], "Fluorescein glows where the surface is missing. Most heal within 1 to 2 days."],
    ["#239B56", "Green-black vomit in an adult with a swollen, tight abdomen", "Bowel obstruction", ["Gastro", "Food poisoning", "Reflux"], "Bilious vomiting means the blockage is below the bile duct. Needs urgent imaging."],
    ["#2E86DE", "Toddler cries, holds their breath, turns blue and goes floppy for seconds, then recovers", "Breath-holding spell", ["Seizure", "Heart problem", "Choking"], "Frightening but harmless. Check for iron deficiency, which makes them more common."],
    ["#5DADE2", "Blue hands and feet in a newborn, pink lips and body", "Acrocyanosis (normal)", ["Heart disease", "Cold injury", "Sepsis"], "Normal in the first days. Blue lips or tongue (central cyanosis) is the worry."],
    ["#2E86C1", "Blue-green urine after surgery to find a sentinel lymph node", "Methylene blue", ["Pseudomonas", "Propofol", "Kidney failure"], "Dyes are passed in the urine. Harmless, but methylene blue can interact with serotonin medicines."],
    ["#3498DB", "Bluish cervix at 8 weeks", "Early pregnancy (Chadwick’s sign)", ["Cervical cancer", "Infection", "Endometriosis"], "Extra blood flow in pregnancy. A pregnancy test is more reliable."],
    ["#1F618D", "Bluish bruising around the belly button in a man with severe upper abdominal pain", "Retroperitoneal bleeding (Cullen’s sign)", ["Hernia", "Bruise from a fall", "Umbilical infection"], "Seen in severe pancreatitis or a ruptured ectopic pregnancy. A late sign."],
    ["#2874A6", "Blue-purple ‘blueberry muffin’ spots in a newborn", "Congenital infection (e.g. CMV or rubella)", ["Bruising from birth", "Mongolian spots", "Haemangioma"], "Blood is being made in the skin. Also seen in some cancers; needs urgent assessment."],
    ["#5499C7", "Blue lips and a pulse oximeter reading of 82% at a ski resort in the Himalayas", "High-altitude hypoxia", ["Asthma", "Cold lips", "Heart attack"], "Air pressure falls with height. Go down if there’s breathlessness at rest or confusion."],
    ["#8E44AD", "Purple raised spots on the legs and buttocks, tummy pain and sore knees in a child", "IgA vasculitis (Henoch–Schönlein purpura)", ["Meningococcal sepsis", "Bruising", "Leukaemia"], "Usually settles, but check urine and blood pressure for kidney involvement for 6 months."],
    ["#7D3C98", "A swollen, painful, purple-blue leg after a big DVT", "Phlegmasia cerulea dolens", ["Cellulitis", "Simple DVT", "Lymphoedema"], "Blocked veins cut off arterial flow. A limb emergency: urgent clot treatment."],
    ["#9B59B6", "Violet, shiny plaques over the nose and cheeks", "Lupus pernio (sarcoidosis)", ["Rosacea", "Lupus", "Frostbite"], "A skin form of sarcoidosis, often with lung and upper airway involvement."],
    ["#A569BD", "Itchy purple-red bumps on the toes after cold, damp weather", "Chilblains (pernio)", ["Frostbite", "Raynaud’s", "Gout"], "An abnormal reaction of small vessels to cold. Keep warm; avoid rapid rewarming."],
    ["#5B2C6F", "Purple, swollen skin with blisters and pain far worse than it looks", "Necrotising fasciitis", ["Cellulitis", "Bruise", "Allergic reaction"], "A surgical emergency. Pain out of proportion is the key early clue."],
    ["#FFB6C1", "Pink, gritty, watery eyes with a tender lump in front of the ear", "Viral conjunctivitis (adenovirus)", ["Bacterial conjunctivitis", "Allergy", "Uveitis"], "Very contagious. Antibiotics don’t help. Wash hands and don’t share towels."],
    ["#F1948A", "Bright pink skin and confusion in someone pulled from a house fire", "Cyanide poisoning", ["Burns", "Sunburn", "Carbon monoxide only"], "Burning plastics release cyanide. Very high lactate is a clue; hydroxocobalamin is the antidote."],
    ["#FADBD8", "Pink, blotchy rash on the trunk just as three days of high fever break, in a baby", "Roseola (HHV-6)", ["Measles", "Antibiotic allergy", "Rubella"], "The rash appears as the fever goes. Harmless; febrile seizures can happen during the fever."],
    ["#F5B7B1", "A pink, pearly lump with a rolled edge and tiny surface vessels on the nose", "Basal cell carcinoma", ["Wart", "Acne", "Seborrhoeic keratosis"], "The most common skin cancer in Australia. Rarely spreads, but grows locally; remove it."],
    ["#EC7063", "A pink, tender lump in a baby’s groin that won’t push back in", "Incarcerated inguinal hernia", ["Swollen lymph node", "Hydrocele", "Undescended testis"], "Needs urgent surgical review. Gentle reduction is often tried first."],
    ["#6E4B3A", "Brown staining of the lower legs above the ankles, with varicose veins", "Venous haemosiderin staining", ["Bruising", "Addison’s disease", "Melanoma"], "Iron from leaked red cells stains the skin. A sign of chronic venous insufficiency; compression helps."],
    ["#7B4B2A", "Brown, warty, ‘stuck-on’ spots on the back of an older person", "Seborrhoeic keratoses", ["Melanoma", "Warts", "Moles"], "Harmless. One that looks different from the rest (‘ugly duckling’) needs checking."],
    ["#A0522D", "A brown line down the middle of the belly in pregnancy", "Linea nigra", ["Addison’s disease", "Bruising", "Melanoma"], "Pregnancy hormones darken skin. It fades after birth."],
    ["#4E342E", "A black-brown, furry-looking tongue after antibiotics", "Black hairy tongue", ["Oral thrush", "Melanoma", "Iron tablets"], "Overgrown tongue papillae trap pigment. Brushing the tongue fixes it."],
    ["#B5651D", "Brown flecks and white spots on children’s teeth in an area with high-fluoride bore water", "Dental fluorosis", ["Tooth decay", "Tetracycline staining", "Iron syrup staining"], "Too much fluoride while teeth are forming. Cosmetic only."],
    ["#6D4C41", "Brown-black dots in a painful sole callus after paring it back", "Plantar wart", ["Corn", "Melanoma", "Splinter"], "The dots are tiny clotted capillaries. Corns don’t have them."],
    ["#1C1C1C", "Black crust on the palate and a swollen face in a person with poorly controlled diabetes", "Mucormycosis", ["Melanoma", "Dental abscess", "Sinusitis only"], "An aggressive fungal infection. Needs surgery and amphotericin urgently."],
    ["#212121", "Black sputum in a retired coal miner", "Coal workers’ pneumoconiosis (melanoptysis)", ["Lung cancer", "Smoking", "Tuberculosis"], "Breakdown of coal dust nodules. Silica exposure also raises TB and lung cancer risk."],
    ["#17202A", "Painless black dots on the heel of a basketball player", "Talon noir (black heel)", ["Melanoma", "Plantar wart", "Splinter"], "Tiny bleeds from shear forces. Paring it away removes the colour; melanoma won’t pare off."],
    ["#2C3E50", "Grey-blue patches on the shins and hard palate after years of antimalarial tablets", "Hydroxychloroquine pigmentation", ["Addison’s disease", "Bruising", "Haemochromatosis"], "Usually on the shins and face. Also needs regular eye checks for retinal toxicity."],
    ["#FDFEFE", "White patches on swollen tonsils, a big spleen and tiredness in a teenager", "Glandular fever (EBV)", ["Strep throat", "Tonsillar cancer", "Thrush"], "Avoid contact sport for at least 3 weeks: the spleen can rupture. Amoxicillin causes a rash."],
    ["#F8F9F9", "Small white spots on the fingernails that grow out", "Leukonychia (minor nail injury)", ["Calcium deficiency", "Zinc deficiency", "Fungal infection"], "Usually from small knocks to the nail base, not low calcium."],
    ["#FFFFFF", "Thick white ‘cottage cheese’ discharge and itch", "Vaginal thrush (candidiasis)", ["Bacterial vaginosis", "Trichomoniasis", "Gonorrhoea"], "Common after antibiotics. Bacterial vaginosis is thin and fishy instead."],
    ["#F4F6F6", "Milky white fluid in a chest drain after heart surgery", "Chylothorax", ["Pus (empyema)", "Pleural effusion", "Blood"], "Lymph leaking from a damaged thoracic duct. High triglycerides in the fluid confirm it."],
    ["#ECF0F1", "White, ridged patches on the sides of the tongue that won’t scrape off, in a person with HIV", "Oral hairy leukoplakia (EBV)", ["Oral thrush", "Lichen planus", "Geographic tongue"], "Harmless itself, but a sign of low immunity."],
    ["#F2F3F4", "Pale, slightly scaly patches on a child’s cheeks after summer", "Pityriasis alba", ["Vitiligo", "Tinea", "Pityriasis versicolor"], "A mild form of eczema. Moisturiser and sunscreen help; it fades."],
    ["#FBFCFC", "Pale patches on the back that don’t tan after a beach holiday, with fine scale", "Pityriasis versicolor", ["Vitiligo", "Pityriasis alba", "Ringworm"], "A yeast (Malassezia) overgrowth. Antifungal shampoo on the skin treats it; colour returns slowly."],
    ["#EAEDED", "White, powdery frost on the skin of a person with untreated kidney failure", "Uraemic frost", ["Salt from sweat", "Fungal infection", "Dry skin"], "Urea crystallises from sweat. Very rare now that dialysis is available."],
    ["#F0F3F4", "Hard white chalky lumps in the fingertips with tight, shiny skin", "Calcinosis (systemic sclerosis)", ["Gout tophi", "Warts", "Heberden’s nodes"], "Part of the CREST pattern of limited systemic sclerosis."],
    ["#E74C3C", "Red, swollen, tender breast in a breastfeeding mum with a fever", "Lactational mastitis", ["Breast cancer", "Blocked duct only", "Shingles"], "Keep feeding or expressing from that side. Antibiotics if it isn’t settling within a day."],
    ["#CB4335", "A red, hot, swollen eyelid with pain on moving the eye and double vision", "Orbital cellulitis", ["Stye", "Allergy", "Preseptal cellulitis"], "Pain on eye movement and double vision mean the infection is behind the eye. Urgent IV antibiotics and CT."],
    ["#D9534F", "Red, raw nappy area that spares the skin creases", "Irritant nappy dermatitis", ["Candida nappy rash", "Psoriasis", "Eczema"], "Urine and poo irritate the exposed skin. Candida loves the creases instead."],
    ["#FF6F61", "Red streaks of blood mixed into stool and diarrhoea for 6 weeks in a 25-year-old", "Inflammatory bowel disease", ["Haemorrhoids", "Gastro", "Irritable bowel syndrome"], "Bloody diarrhoea for weeks needs stool tests, faecal calprotectin and a colonoscopy."],
    ["#EC7063", "A red, smooth patch on the cervix that bleeds after sex, in someone on the pill", "Cervical ectropion", ["Cervical cancer", "Infection", "Polyp"], "Common and harmless with hormones, but check cervical screening is up to date."],
    ["#E35D5B", "Red, itchy, ring-shaped patches on the face of a farmer who works with cattle", "Zoophilic tinea (cattle ringworm)", ["Eczema", "Psoriasis", "Lupus"], "Animal fungi cause angrier rashes. Often needs oral antifungals."],
    ["#F4D03F", "Greasy yellow scale in the eyebrows, sides of the nose and behind the ears", "Seborrhoeic dermatitis", ["Psoriasis", "Rosacea", "Eczema"], "A reaction to Malassezia yeast. Antifungal shampoos and creams help."],
    ["#F7DC6F", "Yellow pus pointing in a red, painful lump on the eyelid edge", "Stye (hordeolum)", ["Chalazion", "Cellulitis", "Basal cell carcinoma"], "Warm compresses usually work. A painless, firm lump is a chalazion instead."],
    ["#D4AC0D", "Yellow-green, smelly discharge from one nostril in a toddler", "Nasal foreign body", ["Sinusitis", "Common cold", "Allergy"], "One-sided, smelly discharge in a small child: look for a bead or a bean."],
    ["#C9A227", "Yellow, waxy, umbilicated papules on a child’s trunk", "Molluscum contagiosum", ["Chickenpox", "Warts", "Milia"], "A pox virus. Harmless and clears within months to a couple of years."],
    ["#239B56", "Green, slimy stools in a toddler who drinks lots of juice and is otherwise well", "Toddler diarrhoea", ["Coeliac disease", "Gastro", "Lactose intolerance"], "Common and harmless. Cut back on juice and add some fat to the diet."],
    ["#C0392B", "Red, warm, swollen knee in a carpet layer who kneels all day", "Prepatellar bursitis (‘housemaid’s knee’)", ["Septic arthritis", "Gout", "Meniscal tear"], "Fluid in the bursa in front of the kneecap. Aspirate if infection is possible."],
    ["#E74C3C", "A red, swollen elbow tip after leaning on a desk for weeks", "Olecranon bursitis", ["Gout of the elbow", "Fracture", "Tennis elbow"], "Usually from pressure. Fever and redness spreading suggest infection."],
    ["#D9534F", "Red, swollen gums that bleed easily in the second trimester", "Pregnancy gingivitis", ["Scurvy", "Leukaemia", "Low platelets"], "Hormones make gums more sensitive. Good brushing and a dental check help."],
    ["#CB4335", "Red, hot, painful lump near the anus with fever", "Perianal abscess", ["Haemorrhoid", "Anal fissure", "Pilonidal sinus"], "Needs drainage; antibiotics alone don’t cure it."],
    ["#B03A2E", "A red, scaly, slow-growing patch on the leg of an older woman that won’t heal", "Squamous cell carcinoma in situ (Bowen’s disease)", ["Eczema", "Psoriasis", "Tinea"], "A non-healing scaly patch on sun-damaged skin needs a biopsy."],
    ["#E6564B", "Red, sore eyelid edges with crusts on the lashes every morning", "Blepharitis", ["Conjunctivitis", "Stye", "Allergy"], "Common and chronic. Daily lid hygiene with warm compresses helps."],
    ["#EC7063", "A red, painful finger nail fold with pus after nail biting", "Acute paronychia", ["Herpetic whitlow", "Felon", "Gout"], "Warm soaks and drainage if there’s pus. Antibiotics only if it’s spreading."],
    ["#F1948A", "Red, burning, clustered blisters on a fingertip of a dental nurse", "Herpetic whitlow", ["Paronychia", "Impetigo", "Burn"], "Herpes simplex. Don’t cut it open; antivirals if early."],
    ["#F4D03F", "Yellow skin and eyes, dark urine and itch, two weeks into a course of flucloxacillin", "Drug-induced cholestasis (flucloxacillin)", ["Hepatitis A", "Gallstones", "Gilbert syndrome"], "Flucloxacillin can cause cholestatic liver injury, sometimes weeks after the course."],
    ["#F9E79F", "Yellow-white specks in an ear canal with itch and fluffy debris", "Otomycosis (fungal ear infection)", ["Earwax", "Bacterial otitis externa", "Cholesteatoma"], "Often after antibiotic ear drops. Cleaning plus antifungal drops."],
    ["#D4AC0D", "A yellow-white pearly mass behind the eardrum and a smelly discharge", "Cholesteatoma", ["Ear infection", "Earwax", "Glue ear"], "Skin growing in the middle ear can erode bone. Needs ENT surgery."],
    ["#F5B041", "Yellow-tinged skin and a lemon-yellow colour in someone with pernicious anaemia", "Pernicious anaemia (lemon-yellow tint)", ["Jaundice from gallstones", "Carotenaemia", "Hypothyroidism"], "Pallor plus mild jaundice from red cells breaking down in the marrow."],
    ["#52BE80", "A green-blue swollen leg after a long-haul flight, now pale and cold", "Arterial embolism", ["DVT", "Cellulitis", "Lymphoedema"], "Pale, cold, pulseless and painful: an emergency. Act within hours."],
    ["#2E86DE", "Bluish swelling of a woman’s inner lip that feels like a soft blister", "Mucocele", ["Melanoma", "Venous lake", "Cold sore"], "A blocked minor salivary gland. Often bursts and returns; can be removed."],
    ["#3867D6", "A soft, dark blue papule on the lower lip of an older man that empties when pressed", "Venous lake", ["Melanoma", "Mucocele", "Kaposi sarcoma"], "A dilated vein from sun damage. Harmless; blanching on pressure is the clue."],
    ["#8E44AD", "A painful purple lump on the palm of a child with a heart murmur and fever", "Osler node (infective endocarditis)", ["Splinter", "Insect bite", "Bruise"], "Painful, tender nodules from immune complexes. Blood cultures and echo."],
    ["#9B59B6", "Purple-red patches on the palms that don’t hurt, in someone with fever and a new murmur", "Janeway lesions (infective endocarditis)", ["Palmar erythema", "Hand, foot and mouth", "Eczema"], "Painless septic emboli. Osler nodes are the painful ones."],
    ["#A569BD", "Purple, swollen tongue and lips after starting a blood pressure medicine", "ACE inhibitor angioedema", ["Anaphylaxis", "Allergy to food", "Infection"], "Bradykinin, not histamine: adrenaline and antihistamines often don’t help. Stop the ACE inhibitor for good."],
    ["#FFB6C1", "Pink, crusted nodule growing fast on the sun-damaged hand of an older man", "Keratoacanthoma", ["Wart", "Basal cell carcinoma", "Insect bite"], "Grows over weeks with a crater. Treated as a squamous cell cancer; remove it."],
    ["#8B5A2B", "Brown patches in the mouth and on the lips of a teenager with tummy pains", "Peutz–Jeghers syndrome", ["Addison’s disease", "Freckles", "Melanoma"], "Pigmented lips plus bowel polyps. Raises bowel and other cancer risks; needs surveillance."],
    ["#A0522D", "Brown, fluid-filled bump at the base of the spine with a hairy dimple", "Pilonidal sinus", ["Boil", "Spina bifida", "Haemorrhoid"], "Hair works into the skin of the natal cleft. Drain abscesses; surgery for recurrent ones."],
    ["#2C3E50", "A black scab on the arm after handling sheep, ringed by swelling, painless", "Cutaneous anthrax", ["Spider bite", "Impetigo", "Burn"], "Rare in Australia but occurs in livestock workers. Painless black eschar with big swelling. Notifiable."],
    ["#17202A", "Black, sticky stool in a patient on iron tablets with a normal blood count", "Iron tablet stool colour", ["Upper GI bleed", "Bowel cancer", "Liquorice"], "Iron darkens stool but it isn’t sticky or tarry like melaena. Check if unsure."],
    ["#F8F9F9", "A painless, firm, white-yellow lump in the middle of the eyelid after a stye", "Chalazion", ["Stye", "Basal cell carcinoma", "Milium"], "A blocked oil gland. Warm compresses; incision if it doesn’t settle."],
    ["#ECF0F1", "White, flat-topped bumps along a scratch line in a child (Koebner)", "Plane warts", ["Lichen planus", "Molluscum", "Milia"], "Flat warts spread along scratches. Usually clear by themselves."],
    ["#F2F3F4", "Pale white earlobe and nose tips after a night in the snow, now numb", "Frostnip progressing to frostbite", ["Raynaud’s", "Chilblains", "Vitiligo"], "Rewarm in warm (not hot) water. Don’t rub; don’t rewarm if refreezing is likely."],
    ["#EAEDED", "White, scaly patch in the groin with satellite spots in a person with diabetes", "Candida intertrigo", ["Tinea cruris", "Psoriasis", "Erythrasma"], "Satellite spots suggest Candida. Keep the area dry; antifungal cream."],
    ["#95A5A6", "Grey, wrinkled fingertips after a long swim", "Normal water wrinkling", ["Raynaud’s", "Dehydration", "Scleroderma"], "A nerve-controlled reflex, probably for grip. Absent wrinkling can be a sign of nerve damage."],
    ["#E74C3C", "Red, itchy, weeping rash on the earlobes and wrist where jewellery touches", "Nickel allergy (allergic contact dermatitis)", ["Eczema", "Psoriasis", "Tinea"], "Patch testing confirms it. Avoid nickel; coat or swap the metal."],
    ["#F39C12", "Orange-brown skin and dark knuckles in a vegan with numb feet", "Vitamin B12 deficiency pigmentation", ["Addison’s disease", "Haemochromatosis", "Melasma"], "B12 deficiency can darken skin, especially knuckles. Strict vegans need B12 supplements."],
    ["#27AE60", "Green-stained fingernails in a dishwasher with a swollen nail fold", "Chronic paronychia with Pseudomonas", ["Fungal nail", "Melanoma", "Bruise"], "Wet work damages the cuticle. Keep hands dry; treat the infection."],
    ["#3498DB", "Blue-black ‘tattoo’ on the gums near an old amalgam filling", "Amalgam tattoo", ["Melanoma", "Bruise", "Lead line"], "Silver filling particles in the gum. Harmless, but biopsy if unsure."],
    ["#8E44AD", "Purple, raised, firm lump that bled after a minor knock, on the gum of a pregnant woman", "Pyogenic granuloma (pregnancy epulis)", ["Gum cancer", "Abscess", "Kaposi sarcoma"], "A vascular overgrowth from hormones. Often shrinks after birth."],
    ["#FDFEFE", "White plaques on the tongue and mouth that wipe off, in someone using a steroid inhaler", "Inhaled steroid oral thrush", ["Leukoplakia", "Lichen planus", "Geographic tongue"], "Rinse and spit after each puff, or use a spacer. Antifungal treatment clears it."],
    ["#C0392B", "Red, burning feet and hands in hot weather that ease in cold water, with a high platelet count", "Erythromelalgia", ["Gout", "Raynaud’s", "Cellulitis"], "Can be linked to blood disorders like essential thrombocythaemia. Aspirin may help in that case."],
    ["#F4D03F", "Yellow, shiny patches on the eyelids of a 30-year-old whose father had a heart attack at 45", "Xanthelasma from familial hypercholesterolaemia", ["Milia", "Sebaceous cysts", "Stye"], "In young people, check lipids: familial hypercholesterolaemia needs early treatment and family testing."],
    ["#2E86C1", "Blue-grey discolouration of the nails and gums on long-term zidovudine (AZT)", "Zidovudine nail pigmentation", ["Cyanosis", "Melanoma", "Fungal infection"], "Drug-induced nail pigmentation; harmless, but a clue to medication history."],
    ["#212121", "Black, ‘walnut’-like cracked skin on the neck and back of a farmer", "Cutis rhomboidalis nuchae (sun damage)", ["Acanthosis nigricans", "Dirt", "Ichthyosis"], "Thick, deeply lined skin from years of sun. A marker of high skin cancer risk."]
